   "act": "state",
   "content": [
    "Once the Railway emergency call is connected and the audible indication is finished, an indication shall be provided to the driver as a reminder of the need to use the Push- To-Talk button on the handset if he wants to speak."
   ]
  },
  {
   "speaker": "Analyst",
   "act": "backchannel"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "Client",
   "act": "state",
   "content": [
    "If a driver is disconnected from the multi-driver call, a clear indication shall be given."
   ]
  }
 ],
 "turns": [
  {
   "id": "M1:T41",
   "speaker": "Analyst",
   "act": "backchannel",
   "guide": "Short acknowledgment while listening (1-3 words)."
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T42",
   "speaker": "EndUser",
   "act": "state",
   "guide": "The speaker states the content in their own words.",
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "The Cab radio shall be capable of being used as a standard telephone, such that the driver is able to call any valid number subject to pre-defined call restrictions. The call may be initiated by: selection from a pre-defined list (up to 99 entries); direct dialling a subscriber number; calling a functional number. Receive incoming point-to-point voice call",
     "role": "statement"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T43",
   "speaker": "Client",
   "act": "state",
   "guide": "The speaker states the content in their own words.",
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "The Cab radio shall provide a means for the driver to terminate calls which he is authorised to terminate (ie all calls except Railway emergency calls not initiated by the driver and shunting group calls).",
     "role": "statement"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T44",
   "speaker": "Analyst",
   "act": "backchannel",
   "guide": "Short acknowledgment while listening (1-3 words)."
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T45",
   "speaker": "EndUser",
   "act": "state",
   "guide": "The speaker states the content in their own words.",
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "For voice calls using the Cab radio not involving the driver as a called or calling party, the driver shall have the possibility to listen to the audio output of the communication.",
     "role": "statement"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T46",
   "speaker": "Analyst",
   "act": "backchannel",
   "guide": "Short acknowledgment while listening (1-3 words)."
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T47",
   "speaker": "Analyst",
   "act": "ask_topic",
   "guide": "Analyst moves the discussion to the topic 'cab radio' and asks about it."
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T48",
   "speaker": "EndUser",
   "act": "state",
   "guide": "The speaker states the content in their own words.",
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "When switched off, the radio shall retain any numbers which are stored at the time the radio is switched off. Switch radio MMI on/off",
     "role": "statement"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T49",
   "speaker": "Client",
   "act": "state",
   "guide": "The speaker states the content in their own words.",
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "If directed network selection and/or automatic network selection are implemented, the driver shall be informed by means of an audible and visual indication of the new network identity whenever a network change takes place without user intervention. Register and deregister train number",
     "role": "statement"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T50",
   "speaker": "EndUser",
   "act": "state",
   "guide": "The speaker states the content in their own words.",
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "Where ERTMS/ETCS and radio systems are available and the driver is required to enter the train number as part of the initialisation procedure, this task shall be carried out only once on the ERTMS/ETCS system and the entered number transmitted to the radio system.",
     "role": "statement"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T51",
   "speaker": "Client",
   "act": "state",
   "guide": "The speaker states the content in their own words.",
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "5.2.3.28ii Data entry may be from either system depending on the operating procedures agreed between the train operator and the railway infrastructure operator.",
     "role": "statement"
    },
    {
     "text": "General MMI functions are required to support the following call functions: forward call to the driver handportable; put a call on hold; display incoming call details whilst in an on-going call; temporarily exit an existing call to answer another incoming call; multi-driver call service.",
     "role": "statement"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T52",
   "speaker": "EndUser",
   "act": "state",
   "guide": "The speaker states the content in their own words.",
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "The Cab radio may need to conserve battery power when the radio is powered up but the MMI is switched off. Handling of call priorities",
     "role": "statement"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T53",
   "speaker": "Analyst",
   "act": "ask_topic",
   "guide": "Analyst moves the discussion to the topic 'environmental and physical requirements' and asks about it."
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T54",
   "speaker": "TechLead",
   "act": "state",
   "guide": "The speaker states the content in their own words.",
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "Train-mounted equipment including the Cab radio terminal equipment, MMI and antenna shall comply with all specifications in section 4.3 and all of those defined in this section.",
     "role": "statement"
    },
    {
     "text": "Measures should be taken to reduce the risk of theft of radio equipment. Examples of such measures include physical protection, alarms and access control measures.",
     "role": "statement"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T55",
   "speaker": "Analyst",
   "act": "ask_topic",
   "guide": "Analyst moves the discussion to the topic 'driver man-machine interface' and asks about it."
